---
import CourseSlideLayout from '../../../../layouts/CourseSlideLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../../../utils/paths';
import '../../../../styles/dedc02-literature-review.css';

const title = '3. Literature Review · DEDC02';
const description = 'An interactive lesson on literature review structure, argumentation, synthesis and citation.';
const courseHref = withBase('/teaching/courses/dedc02');
---

<CourseSlideLayout {title} {description}>
  <section class="pdf-cover" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="eyebrow">DEDC02 · Advanced Research Method</span>
    <h1>Literature<br />Review</h1>
    <div class="pdf-message-block">
      <h2>Personal message</h2>
      <p data-pdf-message-print></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="top-tools" aria-label="Language and timer controls">
    <button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-global-translate>中文</button>
    <div class="compact-timer" aria-label="Activity timer">
      <input type="number" min="0.1" step="0.5" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="Timer" aria-label="Timer duration" data-timer-minutes />
      <output data-timer-output hidden aria-live="polite">00:00</output>
      <button type="button" data-timer-start>Start</button>
      <button type="button" data-timer-reset aria-label="Reset timer">↻</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="deck" aria-label="Literature Review slide deck">
    <section class="slide is-active" data-title="Literature Review" aria-hidden="false">
      <div class="slide-inner title-slide">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">DEDC02 · Advanced Research Method</span></header>
        <div class="title-rule"></div>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h1>Literature<br />Review</h1>
          <p class="lead">Using Toulmin’s model to understand argumentation, then applying it to literature-review structure and paragraph writing.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h1>文獻<br />綜述</h1>
          <p class="lead">運用 Toulmin 模型理解論證，再把它應用於文獻綜述結構與段落寫作。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Learning aims" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Where we are going</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>By the end, you can…</h2>
          <ol class="number-list">
            <li><span><strong>Apply</strong> Toulmin’s claim, grounds, warrant, backing, qualifier and rebuttal.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Design</strong> a coherent chapter and give each section an argumentative purpose.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Build</strong> a paragraph that synthesises evidence and retains your voice.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Decide</strong> why, when and how a source should be cited.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Diagnose</strong> common weaknesses in literature-review writing.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>完成本課後，你可以⋯⋯</h2>
          <ol class="number-list">
            <li><span><strong>運用</strong>Toulmin 模型的主張、Grounds（證據）、論證依據、支持依據、限定語及反駁。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>設計</strong>連貫的章節，並賦予每個小節明確的論證功能。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>建立</strong>能綜合證據並保留作者聲音的段落。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>判斷</strong>為何、何時及如何引用來源。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>診斷</strong>文獻綜述寫作中的常見問題。</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="From search to argument" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Bridge from Week 2</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Searching finds sources. Reviewing builds an argument.</h2>
          <div class="path-line">
            <span>Research question</span><b>→</b><span>Relevant sources</span><b>→</b><span>Patterns and tensions</span><b>→</b><span>Review claim</span>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">The source provides information. The reviewer decides what that information means in relation to other evidence and to the proposed study.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>檢索尋找來源，綜述建立論證。</h2>
          <div class="path-line">
            <span>研究問題</span><b>→</b><span>相關來源</span><b>→</b><span>模式與張力</span><b>→</b><span>綜述主張</span>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">來源提供資料，綜述者則判斷這些資料與其他證據及擬議研究之間的意義。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="What a literature review does" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Purpose</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>What must the review accomplish?</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="purpose-card accent"><h3>Locate</h3><p>Place the study within a larger scholarly conversation.</p></article>
            <article class="purpose-card accent"><h3>Relate</h3><p>Show agreements, contradictions and alternative explanations.</p></article>
            <article class="purpose-card accent"><h3>Evaluate</h3><p>Judge what different evidence can and cannot support.</p></article>
            <article class="purpose-card accent"><h3>Justify</h3><p>Establish the unresolved research space addressed by the study.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>文獻綜述必須完成甚麼？</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="purpose-card accent"><h3>定位</h3><p>把研究置於更廣泛的學術對話中。</p></article>
            <article class="purpose-card accent"><h3>連結</h3><p>呈現一致、矛盾及其他解釋。</p></article>
            <article class="purpose-card accent"><h3>評估</h3><p>判斷不同證據能夠及不能夠支持甚麼。</p></article>
            <article class="purpose-card accent"><h3>論證需要</h3><p>建立本研究將處理的未解研究空間。</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Summary and synthesis" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The central distinction</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Summary reports. Synthesis reorganises.</h2>
          <div class="contrast">
            <article><h3>Paper-by-paper summary</h3><p>Hou et al. (2025) describe a personalised AI tutor. Wang et al. (2025) report a quasi-experiment with AI-based interactive scaffolding.</p></article>
            <b>→</b>
            <article><h3>Synthesis by relationship</h3><p>Together, the papers position AI support as adaptive scaffolding; however, one describes a system and the other tests 60 secondary students, so the strength and scope of their evidence differ (Hou et al., 2025; Wang et al., 2025).</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">A review may summarise individual studies, but its argument comes from comparing, grouping, interpreting and qualifying them.</p>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Vault sources:</strong> Hou et al. (2025), <a href="https://doi.org/10.58379/vchj2886" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.58379/vchj2886</a>; Wang et al. (2025), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>摘要負責報告，綜合負責重組。</h2>
          <div class="contrast">
            <article><h3>逐篇摘要</h3><p>Hou 等人（2025）描述個人化人工智能導師；Wang 等人（2025）報告人工智能互動支架的準實驗。</p></article>
            <b>→</b>
            <article><h3>按關係綜合</h3><p>兩篇論文都把人工智能支援定位為調適性支架；然而，一篇描述系統，另一篇測試 60 名中學生，因此證據力度與適用範圍不同（Hou et al., 2025；Wang et al., 2025）。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">文獻綜述可以摘要個別研究，但其論證來自比較、歸類、詮釋與限定。</p>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Vault 來源：</strong> Hou et al. (2025), <a href="https://doi.org/10.58379/vchj2886" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.58379/vchj2886</a>；Wang et al. (2025), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="What is a claim?" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Argumentation</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>What is a claim?</h2>
          <blockquote>A claim is the point that a writer asks the reader to accept.</blockquote>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel"><h3>Specific</h3><p>Its scope and relationship are clear.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Supportable</h3><p>Relevant evidence could justify it.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Contestable</h3><p>It can be evaluated or qualified.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Purposeful</h3><p>It advances the larger argument.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>甚麼是主張？</h2>
          <blockquote>主張是作者希望讀者接受的觀點。</blockquote>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel"><h3>具體</h3><p>範圍與關係清晰。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>可支持</h3><p>相關證據能夠為其提供理據。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>可質疑</h3><p>主張可以被評估或限定。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>有目的</h3><p>主張推進整體論證。</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="From structure to paragraph" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Where the writing happens</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Structure guides the reader; paragraphs do the reasoning</h2>
          <div class="writing-scales">
            <article><span>Chapter</span><h3>Give the field a clear route</h3><p>Define the scope and order the major strands around the research problem.</p></article>
            <article><span>Section</span><h3>Develop one manageable part</h3><p>Group related literature, compare it and connect the section to the next step.</p></article>
            <article><span>Paragraph</span><h3>Make the reasoning visible</h3><p>State a point, combine sources, explain their relationship and set a boundary.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">We will plan chapters and sections briefly. The main focus is the paragraph, where readers can see what you conclude from the literature and why.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>結構引導讀者；段落展示推理</h2>
          <div class="writing-scales">
            <article><span>章節</span><h3>為研究領域提供清晰路線</h3><p>界定範圍，並圍繞研究問題安排主要脈絡。</p></article>
            <article><span>小節</span><h3>發展一個可處理的部分</h3><p>歸類相關文獻、進行比較，並連結下一步。</p></article>
            <article><span>段落</span><h3>讓推理清晰可見</h3><p>提出觀點、結合來源、解釋關係，並設定邊界。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">我們會簡要規劃章節與小節。主要焦點是段落，因為讀者在這裏看到你從文獻得出甚麼結論，以及理由。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 1: Claim Lab" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 1</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Claim Lab</h2>
          <div class="interactive-stack" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>After adjustment for pre-test scores, the AIIS group had significantly higher vocabulary and goal-setting outcomes than the fixed-scaffolding group (Wang et al., 2025).</p><select data-answer="evidence" aria-label="Classify statement one"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="topic">Topic</option><option value="description">Description</option><option value="evidence">Evidence</option><option value="claim">Review claim</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>AI-based interactive scaffolding may support selected language and self-regulation outcomes for secondary learners in IDLE (Wang et al., 2025).</p><select data-answer="claim" aria-label="Classify statement two"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="topic">Topic</option><option value="description">Description</option><option value="evidence">Evidence</option><option value="claim">Review claim</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>AI-based interactive scaffolding in informal digital learning of English (Wang et al., 2025)</p><select data-answer="topic" aria-label="Classify statement three"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="topic">Topic</option><option value="description">Description</option><option value="evidence">Evidence</option><option value="claim">Review claim</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Wang et al. (2025) compared AI-based interactive scaffolding with fixed scaffolding for 60 secondary students.</p><select data-answer="description" aria-label="Classify statement four"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="topic">Topic</option><option value="description">Description</option><option value="evidence">Evidence</option><option value="claim">Review claim</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>Check answers</button><button type="button" data-clear>Clear</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Vault source:</strong> Wang et al. (2025), <em>Interactive Learning Environments, 33</em>(7), 4633–4652. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>主張實驗室</h2>
          <div class="interactive-stack" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>控制前測分數後，AIIS 組的詞彙與目標設定結果顯著高於固定支架組（Wang et al., 2025）。</p><select data-answer="evidence" aria-label="分類陳述一"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="topic">主題</option><option value="description">描述</option><option value="evidence">證據</option><option value="claim">綜述主張</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>人工智能互動支架可能支援中學生在 IDLE 中的部分語言與自我調節結果（Wang et al., 2025）。</p><select data-answer="claim" aria-label="分類陳述二"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="topic">主題</option><option value="description">描述</option><option value="evidence">證據</option><option value="claim">綜述主張</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>英語非正式數碼學習中的人工智能互動支架（Wang et al., 2025）</p><select data-answer="topic" aria-label="分類陳述三"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="topic">主題</option><option value="description">描述</option><option value="evidence">證據</option><option value="claim">綜述主張</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Wang 等人（2025）比較人工智能互動支架與固定支架對 60 名中學生的影響。</p><select data-answer="description" aria-label="分類陳述四"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="topic">主題</option><option value="description">描述</option><option value="evidence">證據</option><option value="claim">綜述主張</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>檢查答案</button><button type="button" data-clear>清除</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Vault 來源：</strong> Wang et al. (2025), <em>Interactive Learning Environments, 33</em>(7), 4633–4652. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Introducing the Toulmin model" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Argumentation</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Meet the Toulmin model</h2>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>認識 Toulmin 模型</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="video-layout">
          <div class="video-frame">
            <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/GWnEbMZ0IaA?rel=0" title="Toulmin Method video" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
          <aside class="watch-notes" data-language="en">
            <h3>Watch for three questions</h3>
            <ol><li>What does the writer want us to accept?</li><li>What support is offered?</li><li>What connects that support to the claim?</li></ol>
            <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GWnEbMZ0IaA" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open the video on YouTube</a>
            <p class="source-note">Vault reading: Turabian et al. (2007), ch. 5.</p>
          </aside>
          <aside class="watch-notes" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
            <h3>觀看時留意三個問題</h3>
            <ol><li>作者希望我們接受甚麼？</li><li>作者提供了甚麼支持？</li><li>甚麼把這些支持連接到主張？</li></ol>
            <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GWnEbMZ0IaA" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">在 YouTube 開啟影片</a>
            <p class="source-note">Vault 閱讀：Turabian et al. (2007), ch. 5。</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Toulmin model of argument" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Argumentation</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Read the Toulmin model as a connected sentence</h2>
          <div class="toulmin-map connected-toulmin-map" aria-label="Connected Toulmin argument map">
            <details class="tm-grounds tm-evidence tm-expandable" name="toulmin-en">
              <summary><h3>Grounds</h3><small>Evidence · Click to explore</small></summary>
              <p>Reasons, facts or evidence offered to support the claim:</p>
              <ul><li>Empirical findings</li><li>Statistics</li><li>Participant quotations</li><li>Theoretical propositions</li><li>Definitions</li><li>Previous researchers’ interpretations</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>Check:</strong> Is it relevant, sufficient, credible and accurately represented?</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-so" aria-label="so"><span>so</span></div>
            <details class="tm-qualifier tm-expandable" name="toulmin-en">
              <summary><h3>Qualifier</h3><small>Strength and scope · Click</small></summary>
              <p>Shows how certain or widely applicable the claim is.</p>
              <ul><li>Certainty: probably, possibly, likely</li><li>Frequency: usually, often, sometimes</li><li>Scope: most learners, in this context, under these conditions</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>Check:</strong> Does the wording match the strength and boundaries of the grounds?</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-qualifier" aria-label="qualifies the claim"></div>
            <details class="tm-claim tm-expandable" name="toulmin-en">
              <summary><h3>Claim</h3><small>Conclusion · Click to explore</small></summary>
              <p>The assertion the reader is asked to accept.</p>
              <ul><li>A synthesis or interpretation of a pattern</li><li>An evaluation, explanation, implication or unresolved research space</li><li>A claim of fact, value, policy or definition</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>Check:</strong> Is it specific, debatable and supportable rather than merely a topic?</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-since" aria-label="since"><span>since</span></div>
            <details class="tm-warrant tm-expandable" name="toulmin-en">
              <summary><h3>Warrant</h3><small>Reasoning bridge · Click</small></summary>
              <p>The principle or reasoning that makes the move from grounds to claim legitimate.</p>
              <ul><li>A theoretical or disciplinary assumption</li><li>Causal, comparative or generalisation logic</li><li>An interpretive rule explaining why the evidence matters</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>Ask:</strong> Why do these grounds justify this particular claim?</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-because" aria-label="because"><span>because</span></div>
            <details class="tm-backing tm-expandable" name="toulmin-en">
              <summary><h3>Backing</h3><small>Support for warrant · Click</small></summary>
              <p>Additional support showing that the warrant is reliable or acceptable.</p>
              <ul><li>Established theory or disciplinary principles</li><li>Prior research validating the assumed relationship</li><li>Authoritative definitions, mechanisms or methodological knowledge</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>Check:</strong> Does it support the reasoning bridge, rather than merely repeat the grounds?</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-unless" aria-label="unless"><span>unless</span></div>
            <details class="tm-rebuttal tm-expandable" name="toulmin-en">
              <summary><h3>Rebuttal</h3><small>Exceptions and limits · Click</small></summary>
              <p>Conditions under which the claim or reasoning may not hold.</p>
              <ul><li>Contradictory findings or counterexamples</li><li>Alternative explanations or interpretations</li><li>Populations, contexts or conditions that form exceptions</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>Check:</strong> Has the writer acknowledged and answered the strongest credible challenge?</p>
            </details>
          </div>
          <p class="tm-reading"><strong>Read it:</strong> Grounds, <em>so</em> (Qualifier) Claim, <em>since</em> Warrant, <em>because</em> Backing, <em>unless</em> Rebuttal. <small>Vault reading: Turabian et al. (2007), ch. 5.</small></p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>把 Toulmin 模型讀成一個相連的句子</h2>
          <div class="toulmin-map connected-toulmin-map" aria-label="相連的 Toulmin 論證地圖">
            <details class="tm-grounds tm-evidence tm-expandable" name="toulmin-zh">
              <summary><h3>Grounds（證據）</h3><small>點擊查看證據類型</small></summary>
              <p>用以支持主張的理由、事實或證據：</p>
              <ul><li>實證研究發現</li><li>統計數據</li><li>參與者引語</li><li>理論命題</li><li>定義</li><li>先前研究者的詮釋</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>檢查：</strong>證據是否相關、充分、可信並得到準確呈現？</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-so" aria-label="所以"><span>所以</span></div>
            <details class="tm-qualifier tm-expandable" name="toulmin-zh">
              <summary><h3>限定語</h3><small>力度與範圍 · 點擊查看</small></summary>
              <p>表示主張的確定程度及適用範圍。</p>
              <ul><li>確定程度：很可能、也許、似乎</li><li>頻率：通常、經常、有時</li><li>範圍：多數學習者、在此情境下、在這些條件下</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>檢查：</strong>措辭是否符合證據的力度與邊界？</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-qualifier" aria-label="限定主張的力度與範圍"></div>
            <details class="tm-claim tm-expandable" name="toulmin-zh">
              <summary><h3>主張</h3><small>結論 · 點擊查看</small></summary>
              <p>希望讀者接受的論斷。</p>
              <ul><li>對某一模式的綜合或詮釋</li><li>評價、解釋、含義或尚未解決的研究空間</li><li>事實、價值、政策或定義類主張</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>檢查：</strong>它是否具體、可辯論且可支持，而不只是一個主題？</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-since" aria-label="因為"><span>因為</span></div>
            <details class="tm-warrant tm-expandable" name="toulmin-zh">
              <summary><h3>論證依據</h3><small>推理橋樑 · 點擊查看</small></summary>
              <p>使 Grounds 能夠合理導向主張的原則或推理。</p>
              <ul><li>理論或學科假設</li><li>因果、比較或概括邏輯</li><li>解釋證據為何重要的詮釋規則</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>提問：</strong>為甚麼這些 Grounds 能證成這一特定主張？</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-because" aria-label="因為"><span>因為</span></div>
            <details class="tm-backing tm-expandable" name="toulmin-zh">
              <summary><h3>支持依據</h3><small>支持推理 · 點擊查看</small></summary>
              <p>進一步說明論證依據為何可靠或可接受。</p>
              <ul><li>公認理論或學科原則</li><li>驗證所假定關係的先前研究</li><li>權威定義、機制或方法知識</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>檢查：</strong>它是否支持推理橋樑，而非只是重複 Grounds？</p>
            </details>
            <div class="tm-link tm-link-unless" aria-label="除非"><span>除非</span></div>
            <details class="tm-rebuttal tm-expandable" name="toulmin-zh">
              <summary><h3>反駁</h3><small>例外與限制 · 點擊查看</small></summary>
              <p>主張或推理可能不成立的條件。</p>
              <ul><li>相反研究發現或反例</li><li>其他解釋或詮釋</li><li>構成例外的人群、情境或條件</li></ul>
              <p class="tm-question"><strong>檢查：</strong>作者是否承認並回應最有力且可信的挑戰？</p>
            </details>
          </div>
          <p class="tm-reading"><strong>讀法：</strong>Grounds（證據），<em>所以</em>（限定語）主張，<em>因為</em>論證依據，論證依據成立<em>因為</em>有支持依據，<em>除非</em>出現反駁條件。<small>Vault 閱讀：Turabian et al. (2007), ch. 5。</small></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

