    <section class="slide" data-title="A flexible chapter architecture" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Chapter level</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>A flexible architecture</h2>
          <div class="architecture">
            <article><span>01</span><p><strong>Introduction</strong><br />Purpose, scope and route</p></article>
            <article><span>02</span><p><strong>Key concepts</strong><br />Definitions and boundaries</p></article>
            <article><span>03</span><p><strong>Major strands</strong><br />Themes, debates or relationships</p></article>
            <article><span>04</span><p><strong>Framework</strong><br />Theory and concepts</p></article>
            <article><span>05</span><p><strong>Evidence</strong><br />Methodological strengths and limits</p></article>
            <article><span>06</span><p><strong>Research space</strong><br />Uncertainty, tension or gap</p></article>
            <article><span>07</span><p><strong>Conclusion</strong><br />Synthesis and link to the study</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>可調整的章節架構</h2>
          <div class="architecture">
            <article><span>01</span><p><strong>引言</strong><br />目的、範圍與路線</p></article>
            <article><span>02</span><p><strong>核心概念</strong><br />定義與邊界</p></article>
            <article><span>03</span><p><strong>主要脈絡</strong><br />主題、爭論或關係</p></article>
            <article><span>04</span><p><strong>框架</strong><br />理論與概念</p></article>
            <article><span>05</span><p><strong>證據</strong><br />方法上的優點與限制</p></article>
            <article><span>06</span><p><strong>研究空間</strong><br />不確定、張力或缺口</p></article>
            <article><span>07</span><p><strong>結論</strong><br />綜合並連結本研究</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Organising strategies" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Chapter level</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Choose an organising logic</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Thematic</h3><p>Organise around recurring issues, concepts or debates.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Chronological</h3><p>Trace a meaningful development across time, not merely publication dates.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Methodological</h3><p>Compare how different designs produce different kinds of evidence.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Theoretical</h3><p>Compare explanatory lenses, assumptions and propositions.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">A chapter may combine strategies. Name the principal logic and use another only when it helps the reader follow the argument.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>選擇組織邏輯</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>主題式</h3><p>按反覆出現的議題、概念或爭論組織。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>時間式</h3><p>追蹤隨時間出現的實質發展，而非只按出版年份排列。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>方法式</h3><p>比較不同設計如何產生不同種類的證據。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>理論式</h3><p>比較解釋視角、假設與命題。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">一章可以結合多種策略，但應指出主要邏輯；只有在有助讀者理解論證時才加入其他策略。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Section-level structure" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Section level</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Give each section one clear job</h2>
          <div class="section-flow">
            <article><span>Focus</span><p>Name the issue, relationship or debate this section addresses.</p></article>
            <article><span>Group</span><p>Bring relevant studies together by pattern rather than by author.</p></article>
            <article><span>Compare</span><p>Show where findings, concepts or methods converge and diverge.</p></article>
            <article><span>Evaluate</span><p>Judge the strength, limits and relevance of the available evidence.</p></article>
            <article><span>Conclude</span><p>State what can reasonably be concluded from this body of work.</p></article>
            <article><span>Connect</span><p>Show why the next section or the proposed study is needed.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">These are functions, not a fixed six-paragraph template. A short section may combine several functions.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>賦予每個小節一項清晰任務</h2>
          <div class="section-flow">
            <article><span>聚焦</span><p>指出本節處理的議題、關係或爭論。</p></article>
            <article><span>歸類</span><p>按模式而非按作者組合相關研究。</p></article>
            <article><span>比較</span><p>顯示發現、概念或方法在哪裏一致或分歧。</p></article>
            <article><span>評估</span><p>判斷現有證據的強度、限制與相關性。</p></article>
            <article><span>結論</span><p>說明根據這些文獻可以合理得出甚麼結論。</p></article>
            <article><span>連結</span><p>說明為何需要下一節或擬議研究。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">這些是功能，不是固定的六段模板。較短的小節可以結合多項功能。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Evidence roles" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Section level</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Sources do different argumentative work</h2>
          <div class="grid-6">
            <article class="source-role"><h3>Support</h3><p>Provides findings consistent with the emerging conclusion.</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>Explain</h3><p>Offers a concept or theory that helps interpret a pattern.</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>Qualify</h3><p>Adds a condition, boundary or degree of certainty.</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>Contrast</h3><p>Shows how another population, context or method differs.</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>Challenge</h3><p>Offers contrary evidence or an exception.</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>Extend</h3><p>Suggests a new implication, perspective or research direction.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Do not ask only, “What did this paper find?” Ask, “What role does it play in my argument?”</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>不同來源承擔不同論證功能</h2>
          <div class="grid-6">
            <article class="source-role"><h3>支持</h3><p>提供與逐漸形成的結論一致的發現。</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>解釋</h3><p>提供有助於詮釋模式的概念或理論。</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>限定</h3><p>加入條件、邊界或確定程度。</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>對比</h3><p>顯示另一人群、情境或方法如何不同。</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>挑戰</h3><p>提出相反證據或例外。</p></article>
            <article class="source-role"><h3>延伸</h3><p>提出新的啟示、視角或研究方向。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">不要只問「這篇文章發現了甚麼？」還要問「它在我的論證中扮演甚麼角色？」</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Critical evaluation" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Section level</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Critical does not mean negative</h2>
          <div class="evaluation-grid">
            <article><h3>Provenance</h3><p>Who produced the evidence, with what expertise and data?</p></article>
            <article><h3>Objectivity</h3><p>Were alternatives, contrary evidence and assumptions considered?</p></article>
            <article><h3>Persuasiveness</h3><p>Do the evidence and reasoning justify the conclusion?</p></article>
            <article><h3>Value</h3><p>What does this work contribute to this particular review?</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Evaluate the fitness of evidence for a claim. A limited study may still have conceptual, methodological or historical value.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>批判不等於負面</h2>
          <div class="evaluation-grid">
            <article><h3>來源背景</h3><p>誰以甚麼專業知識與數據產生這項證據？</p></article>
            <article><h3>客觀性</h3><p>是否考慮其他觀點、相反證據與假設？</p></article>
            <article><h3>說服力</h3><p>證據與推理是否足以支持結論？</p></article>
            <article><h3>價值</h3><p>這項工作對本次綜述有何貢獻？</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">評估證據是否適合支持主張。一項有限制的研究仍可能具有概念、方法或歷史價值。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

