    <section class="slide" data-title="Published paragraph A" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Paragraph investigation · Published example A</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>What is this paragraph doing?</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Read the complete published paragraph once. Then analyse it sentence by sentence: What is the controlling point? How are sources related? What does the writer add? Open each note only after your group agrees.</p>
          <div class="sentence-analysis-list published-paragraph">
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>1</span> The number of academic and commercial tools for language learning is growing rapidly, e.g., popular systems such as Duolingo, Rosetta Stone, Babbel, Busuu, and iTalki.</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Establishes the topic through examples, but the broad growth claim is not cited and the sentence does not yet state an analytical point.</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>2</span> Some CALL systems aim to give learners access to authentic materials (White &amp; Reinders, 2010), the opportunity to interact with teachers and native speakers (e.g., the app Lingoda is a platform for live video classes) and provide text or audio feedback based on learner needs and knowledge (Bodnar et al., 2017).</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Lists several affordances. The long coordination and uneven citation placement make it difficult to see precisely which source supports which proposition.</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>3</span> Modern CALL systems are also mobile, which increases their accessibility (Derakhshan &amp; Khodabakhshzadeh, 2011; Kacetl &amp; Klímová, 2019; Rosell-Aguilar, 2018).</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Adds another feature and a claimed consequence. The relation between mobility and the paragraph’s earlier list remains implicit.</p></details>
            <details class="paragraph-verdict"><summary>Reveal a possible overall judgement</summary><p>For the purpose of an argumentative literature review, this paragraph is mainly descriptive: it inventories tools and affordances but offers little synthesis, evaluation or explicit connection to a research problem. That does not make it unusable; it may serve as brief background when description is the writer’s immediate purpose.</p></details>
          </div>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Quoted from:</strong> Hou, J., Vu, A.-D., Katinskaia, A., &amp; Yangarber, R. (2025). AI-assisted second-language teaching and learning in the Zone of Proximal Development. <em>Studies in Language Assessment, 14</em>(2), 92–122. <a href="https://doi.org/10.58379/vchj2886" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://doi.org/10.58379/vchj2886</a> (p. 96).</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>這個段落在做甚麼？</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">先完整閱讀已發表的原文段落，再逐句分析：控制觀點是甚麼？來源如何互相連結？作者加入了甚麼？小組達成共識後才打開提示。</p>
          <div class="sentence-analysis-list published-paragraph">
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>1</span> The number of academic and commercial tools for language learning is growing rapidly, e.g., popular systems such as Duolingo, Rosetta Stone, Babbel, Busuu, and iTalki.</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>以例子建立主題，但「快速增長」這項廣泛主張沒有引用，也尚未提出分析觀點。</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>2</span> Some CALL systems aim to give learners access to authentic materials (White &amp; Reinders, 2010), the opportunity to interact with teachers and native speakers (e.g., the app Lingoda is a platform for live video classes) and provide text or audio feedback based on learner needs and knowledge (Bodnar et al., 2017).</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>列出多種功能。句子並列過長，引用位置又不一致，因此難以判斷每個來源準確支持哪一項命題。</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>3</span> Modern CALL systems are also mobile, which increases their accessibility (Derakhshan &amp; Khodabakhshzadeh, 2011; Kacetl &amp; Klímová, 2019; Rosell-Aguilar, 2018).</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>增加另一項特徵及其影響，但「流動性」與前述清單的關係仍然隱含。</p></details>
            <details class="paragraph-verdict"><summary>顯示一個可能的整體判斷</summary><p>若以論證型文獻綜述為目的，這個段落主要是描述性的：它列舉工具與功能，但較少綜合、評估或明確連結研究問題。這不代表段落完全不可用；當作者當下的目的是提供簡短背景時，這種描述仍可能合適。</p></details>
          </div>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>引文來源：</strong> Hou, J., Vu, A.-D., Katinskaia, A., &amp; Yangarber, R. (2025). AI-assisted second-language teaching and learning in the Zone of Proximal Development. <em>Studies in Language Assessment, 14</em>(2), 92–122. <a href="https://doi.org/10.58379/vchj2886" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://doi.org/10.58379/vchj2886</a>（p. 96）。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Published paragraph B" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Paragraph investigation · Published example B</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Watch the argument develop</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Trace the paragraph’s movement from claim to evidence, interpretation and research space. Analyse every sentence before opening its note.</p>
          <div class="sentence-analysis-list published-paragraph compact-paragraph">
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>1</span> Less is known about the developmental trajectories (i.e. pathways) of secondary students’ goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation with AIIS in IDLE.</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Opens with a knowledge-gap claim and defines its population, processes and context.</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>2</span> Adolescence has been considered as a turning point for developing metacognitive monitoring, reflection, and regulatory skills, so it is expected that adolescents’ goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation should gradually increase (Bardach et al., 2023).</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Supplies a theoretically informed expectation and places the citation beside the proposition that supports it.</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>3</span> However, relevant studies indicated mixed potential trajectories, especially in new learning environments.</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> “However” turns from the expectation to a tension in the empirical literature.</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>4</span> For example, when new learning environments presented cognitive learning difficulty, the levels of learners’ self-rated attainment such as goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation tended to decrease from the beginning until the third or seventh month, followed by a stabilizing trend afterwards (Koizumi &amp; Matsuo, 1993).</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Provides a concrete declining-and-stabilising pattern as Grounds for the tension.</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>5</span> This decline-and-stabilizing trend reflected the process that the learners adjusted their goals based on self-evaluation until the goal scores came to approach their latest learning performance.</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Interprets what the reported pattern may mean rather than merely adding another finding.</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>6</span> Moreover, a rising trend was found in goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation in online learning (Chiu, 2023).</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Adds a contrasting pattern, making the earlier statement about mixed trajectories visible.</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>7</span> While these studies suggested potential developmental trajectories, in the specific context of using AIIS for secondary students’ speaking learning in IDLE, the developmental trajectories are unknown.</summary><p><strong>Possible analysis:</strong> Synthesises the preceding evidence, qualifies what it establishes and narrows the unresolved research space.</p></details>
            <details class="paragraph-verdict"><summary>Reveal a possible overall judgement</summary><p>For this lesson’s purpose, this is the more argumentative paragraph: its sentences establish a gap, develop an expectation, contrast empirical patterns, interpret one pattern and return to a carefully bounded gap. A critical reader should still ask how the opening “less is known” claim was established.</p></details>
          </div>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Quoted from:</strong> Wang, F., Zhou, X., Li, K., Cheung, A. C. K., &amp; Tian, M. (2025). The effects of artificial intelligence-based interactive scaffolding on secondary students’ speaking performance, goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation in informal digital learning of English. <em>Interactive Learning Environments, 33</em>(7), 4633–4652. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a> (p. 4637).</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>觀察論證如何發展</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">追蹤段落如何從主張推進至證據、詮釋與研究空間。打開提示前，先逐句分析。</p>
          <div class="sentence-analysis-list published-paragraph compact-paragraph">
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>1</span> Less is known about the developmental trajectories (i.e. pathways) of secondary students’ goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation with AIIS in IDLE.</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>以知識缺口主張開始，並界定人群、過程與情境。</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>2</span> Adolescence has been considered as a turning point for developing metacognitive monitoring, reflection, and regulatory skills, so it is expected that adolescents’ goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation should gradually increase (Bardach et al., 2023).</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>提出有理論支持的預期，並把引用放在它所支持的命題旁邊。</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>3</span> However, relevant studies indicated mixed potential trajectories, especially in new learning environments.</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>「However」把論述從理論預期轉向實證文獻中的張力。</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>4</span> For example, when new learning environments presented cognitive learning difficulty, the levels of learners’ self-rated attainment such as goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation tended to decrease from the beginning until the third or seventh month, followed by a stabilizing trend afterwards (Koizumi &amp; Matsuo, 1993).</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>提供先下降、後穩定的具體模式，作為呈現張力的 Grounds。</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>5</span> This decline-and-stabilizing trend reflected the process that the learners adjusted their goals based on self-evaluation until the goal scores came to approach their latest learning performance.</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>詮釋已報告的模式可能意味著甚麼，而非只加入另一項發現。</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>6</span> Moreover, a rising trend was found in goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation in online learning (Chiu, 2023).</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>加入相反模式，使前文所指的「混合軌跡」清晰可見。</p></details>
            <details class="sentence-analysis"><summary><span>7</span> While these studies suggested potential developmental trajectories, in the specific context of using AIIS for secondary students’ speaking learning in IDLE, the developmental trajectories are unknown.</summary><p><strong>可能分析：</strong>綜合前述證據、限定它能支持的結論，並收窄尚未解決的研究空間。</p></details>
            <details class="paragraph-verdict"><summary>顯示一個可能的整體判斷</summary><p>以本課目的而言，這個段落更具論證性：各句先建立缺口，再發展預期、對比實證模式、詮釋其中一種模式，最後返回範圍清楚的研究缺口。批判性讀者仍應追問開首「所知較少」的主張如何被確立。</p></details>
          </div>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>引文來源：</strong> Wang, F., Zhou, X., Li, K., Cheung, A. C. K., &amp; Tian, M. (2025). The effects of artificial intelligence-based interactive scaffolding on secondary students’ speaking performance, goal setting, self-evaluation, and motivation in informal digital learning of English. <em>Interactive Learning Environments, 33</em>(7), 4633–4652. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>（p. 4637）。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Paragraph focus and citation emphasis" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Paragraph level</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Do not let author names control the paragraph</h2>
          <p class="intro-line"><strong>How you cite changes the emphasis.</strong> Narrative citations foreground researchers; parenthetical citations foreground the proposition.</p>
          <div class="contrast">
            <article><h3>Source-led + narrative</h3><p><strong>Hou et al. (2025)</strong> describe a personalised tutor. <strong>Wang et al. (2025)</strong> examine interactive scaffolding. <strong>Zhai and Ma (2022)</strong> model students’ acceptance of AWE.</p><p class="source-note">The researchers remain the grammatical subjects and control the paragraph.</p></article>
            <b>→</b>
            <article><h3>Claim-led + parenthetical</h3><p>AI-mediated support has been framed as personalised scaffolding (Hou et al., 2025), tested for selected learning outcomes (Wang et al., 2025), and examined through learners’ acceptance of automated feedback systems (Zhai &amp; Ma, 2022).</p><p class="source-note">The proposition controls the sentence; citations show which sources support each part.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction">Use narrative citation when the researcher or study matters. Use parenthetical citation when the relationship across the literature should stay in the foreground.</p>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Vault sources:</strong> Hou et al. (2025), <a href="https://doi.org/10.58379/vchj2886" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.58379/vchj2886</a>; Wang et al. (2025), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>; Zhai &amp; Ma (2022), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/09588221.2021.1897019" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/09588221.2021.1897019</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>不要讓作者姓名控制段落</h2>
          <p class="intro-line"><strong>引用方式會改變重點。</strong>敘述式引用突出研究者；括號式引用突出命題。</p>
          <div class="contrast">
            <article><h3>來源主導＋敘述式</h3><p><strong>Hou 等人（2025）</strong>描述個人化導師；<strong>Wang 等人（2025）</strong>檢視互動支架；<strong>Zhai 與 Ma（2022）</strong>建立學生接受 AWE 的模型。</p><p class="source-note">研究者一直擔任語法主語，因而控制段落。</p></article>
            <b>→</b>
            <article><h3>主張主導＋括號式</h3><p>人工智能支援被界定為個人化支架（Hou et al., 2025）、被測試對部分學習結果的作用（Wang et al., 2025），亦從學習者接受自動回饋系統的角度被研究（Zhai &amp; Ma, 2022）。</p><p class="source-note">命題控制句子；引用指出每個部分由哪些來源支持。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction">當研究者或研究本身重要時，使用敘述式引用。當文獻之間的關係應保持在前景時，使用括號式引用。</p>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Vault 來源：</strong> Hou et al. (2025), <a href="https://doi.org/10.58379/vchj2886" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.58379/vchj2886</a>；Wang et al. (2025), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>；Zhai &amp; Ma (2022), <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/09588221.2021.1897019" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/09588221.2021.1897019</a>。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Why cite?" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Citation as scholarly practice</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Why cite?</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="citation-card"><h3>Credit</h3><p>Acknowledge the intellectual work of others.</p></article>
            <article class="citation-card"><h3>Evidence</h3><p>Show which source supplies the evidence for a claim.</p></article>
            <article class="citation-card"><h3>Borrowed ideas</h3><p>Identify theories, definitions, methods and interpretations that come from others.</p></article>
            <article class="citation-card"><h3>Traceability</h3><p>Enable readers to locate and evaluate the source.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">A citation identifies where material comes from. It does not explain the relationship between sources or repair weak reasoning.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>為甚麼要引用？</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="citation-card"><h3>承認貢獻</h3><p>承認他人的知識工作。</p></article>
            <article class="citation-card"><h3>證據</h3><p>顯示哪個來源為主張提供證據。</p></article>
            <article class="citation-card"><h3>借用的觀點</h3><p>指出來自他人的理論、定義、方法與詮釋。</p></article>
            <article class="citation-card"><h3>可追溯性</h3><p>讓讀者找到並評估來源。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">引用指出材料來自哪裏。它不會解釋來源之間的關係，也不能修補薄弱推理。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="When to cite" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Citation decisions</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>When should you cite?</h2>
          <div class="do-dont">
            <article><h3>Cite</h3><ul><li>Source-specific facts, statistics or findings</li><li>Theories, models, concepts and definitions</li><li>Methods or interpretive principles borrowed from others</li><li>Paraphrased, summarised or quoted ideas</li><li>Limitations, contrasts or interpretations derived from particular studies</li></ul></article>
            <article><h3>Usually no citation</h3><ul><li>Your clearly identified research decision</li><li>Your own transition or analytical implication</li><li>Genuinely common knowledge for the intended readers</li></ul></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Common knowledge depends on audience and discipline. When uncertain, ask whose idea or evidence the sentence depends upon.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>何時應該引用？</h2>
          <div class="do-dont">
            <article><h3>需要引用</h3><ul><li>特定來源的事實、統計或發現</li><li>理論、模型、概念與定義</li><li>借用自他人的方法或詮釋原則</li><li>改寫、摘要或直接引用他人的觀點</li><li>源自特定研究的限制、對比或詮釋</li></ul></article>
            <article><h3>通常毋須引用</h3><ul><li>已清楚標示為你的研究決定</li><li>你自己的過渡或分析含義</li><li>對目標讀者而言真正屬於常識的內容</li></ul></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">常識取決於讀者與學科。如有疑問，問這句話依賴誰的觀點或證據。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Paraphrase and quotation" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Using sources</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Paraphrase and quote with precision</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Choose the form that preserves the source accurately and serves your reason for using it.</p>
          <div class="citation-scope">
            <article><strong>Paraphrase</strong><p>Represent the source accurately in your own wording and cite it.</p></article>
            <article><strong>Short quote</strong><p>Use quotation marks and include author, year and page or paragraph location.</p></article>
            <article><strong>40+ words</strong><p>Use an indented block quotation without quotation marks; quote only when the exact wording matters.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>準確改寫與直接引用</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">選擇能準確保留來源意思，並符合你使用目的的方式。</p>
          <div class="citation-scope">
            <article><strong>改寫</strong><p>以自己的措辭準確表達來源內容，並提供引用。</p></article>
            <article><strong>短引語</strong><p>使用引號，並包括作者、年份及頁碼或段落位置。</p></article>
            <article><strong>40 字以上</strong><p>使用縮排的區塊引文，不加引號；只有在原文措辭重要時才直接引用。</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Citation placement and scope" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Citation decisions</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Make the citation’s scope visible</h2>
          <div class="citation-scope">
            <article><strong>Close</strong><p>Place the citation immediately beside the idea or evidence it supports.</p></article>
            <article><strong>Accurate</strong><p>Do not group sources as agreeing unless each supports the stated proposition.</p></article>
            <article><strong>Primary</strong><p>When practical, read and cite the original theory or study instead of repeating a secondary claim.</p></article>
            <article><strong>Selective</strong><p>Cite enough to support the claim, but do not replace synthesis with a pile of references.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">A single citation at the end of a long paragraph may leave the reader unable to tell which sentences it supports.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>清楚顯示引用的涵蓋範圍</h2>
          <div class="citation-scope">
            <article><strong>接近</strong><p>把引用放在它所支持的觀點或證據旁邊。</p></article>
            <article><strong>準確</strong><p>除非每個來源都支持該命題，否則不要把它們列為一致。</p></article>
            <article><strong>原始來源</strong><p>可行情況下，閱讀並引用原始理論或研究，而非轉述二手主張。</p></article>
            <article><strong>選擇性</strong><p>提供足以支持主張的引用，但不要用大量文獻取代綜合。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">在長段落結尾只放一項引用，可能令讀者無法判斷它支持哪些句子。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

