    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Research gaps" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From synthesis to research space</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>A gap is an argued conclusion</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Theoretical</h3><p>An existing explanation is incomplete or conflicting.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Empirical</h3><p>Relevant evidence is limited, inconsistent or absent.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Methodological</h3><p>Existing designs cannot answer an important aspect of the problem.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Contextual</h3><p>Populations, places or periods are systematically under-represented.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Do not declare “no research exists” after a quick search. Show the pattern, its consequence and why your study is an appropriate response.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>缺口是經論證得出的結論</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>理論缺口</h3><p>現有解釋並不完整或互相衝突。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>實證缺口</h3><p>相關證據有限、不一致或缺失。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>方法缺口</h3><p>現有設計無法回答研究課題的重要面向。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>情境缺口</h3><p>某些人群、地點或時期長期代表不足。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">不要在快速檢索後便宣稱「沒有研究」。應呈現證據模式、其後果，以及你的研究為何是合適回應。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Common mistakes" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Quality check</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Common literature-review failures</h2>
          <div class="grid-6">
            <article class="panel"><h3>Loose relevance</h3><p>Interesting sources do not clearly serve the research problem.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Paper dumping</h3><p>Studies are reported separately without synthesis.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Uncritical acceptance</h3><p>Published conclusions are treated as automatically valid.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Confirmation bias</h3><p>Only supportive evidence is included.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Invisible method</h3><p>Selection and search procedures are not explained.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Citation fog</h3><p>The reader cannot see which source supports which claim.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>文獻綜述的常見問題</h2>
          <div class="grid-6">
            <article class="panel"><h3>關聯鬆散</h3><p>有趣的來源未能清楚服務研究課題。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>堆砌文獻</h3><p>逐篇報告研究，沒有綜合。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>不加批判地接受</h3><p>把已出版結論視為必然有效。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>確認偏誤</h3><p>只納入支持既有看法的證據。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>方法不可見</h3><p>沒有解釋選擇與檢索程序。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>引用迷霧</h3><p>讀者無法看出哪個來源支持哪項主張。</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 4: Review Debugger" data-delayed-debug-reveal aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 4</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Literature Review Debugger</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Before opening a card, name the writing problem and propose a repair.</p>
          <div class="debug-grid">
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>“Wang et al. (2025) prove that AIIS improves speaking.”</summary><p>Overclaiming: overall speaking was not significantly different, and the authors caution that the sample was small.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>One source is summarised for half a page.</summary><p>Keep only information that serves the section claim. Relate it to other evidence and explain its role.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>A paragraph contains six citations but no clear point.</summary><p>No controlling point: state what the sources collectively show, group them by relationship and explain your interpretation.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>“No study has examined this topic.”</summary><p>Unsupported absolute claim: report the pattern found through a transparent search and define the search coverage.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>A paraphrase changes words but copies the source structure.</summary><p>Return to the meaning, close the source, restate the idea accurately in a new structure and still cite it.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>Only evidence supporting the preferred theory is included.</summary><p>Selective synthesis: search for contrary findings and alternative explanations, then use them to refine the conclusion.</p></details>
          </div>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Vault basis:</strong> The overclaiming case uses Wang et al. (2025); the other diagnostic tasks apply the research-writing guidance in Turabian et al. (2007). <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>文獻綜述除錯器</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">打開卡片前，小組先指出寫作問題，並提出修正方法。</p>
          <div class="debug-grid">
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>「Wang 等人（2025）證明 AIIS 能改善口語。」</summary><p>過度主張：整體口語結果沒有顯著差異，而且作者提醒樣本規模較小。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>用半頁摘要單一來源。</summary><p>只保留服務小節主張的資料；把它與其他證據連結並解釋其角色。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>一個段落有六項引用，但沒有清晰觀點。</summary><p>沒有控制觀點：先說明來源共同顯示甚麼，按關係歸類，並解釋你的詮釋。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>「沒有研究探討此主題。」</summary><p>缺乏支持的絕對主張：報告透明檢索所顯示的模式，並界定檢索覆蓋範圍。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>改寫只更換詞語，卻複製來源結構。</summary><p>回到意思，關閉來源，以新結構準確重述，並仍然提供引用。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>只納入支持偏好理論的證據。</summary><p>選擇性綜合：搜尋相反發現與其他解釋，再用它們細化結論。</p></details>
          </div>
          <p class="paper-citation"><strong>Vault 依據：</strong> 過度主張案例採用 Wang et al. (2025)；其餘除錯任務應用 Turabian et al. (2007) 的研究寫作指引。<a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi:10.1080/10494820.2025.2470319</a>。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Paragraph audit" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Integration</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Run a final paragraph audit</h2>
          <div class="paragraph-audit">
            <article><span>1</span><p><strong>Point</strong><br />Is one clear idea controlling the paragraph?</p></article>
            <article><span>2</span><p><strong>Selection</strong><br />Does every source serve that point?</p></article>
            <article><span>3</span><p><strong>Synthesis</strong><br />Are sources compared rather than listed?</p></article>
            <article><span>4</span><p><strong>Interpretation</strong><br />Have you explained what the pattern means?</p></article>
            <article><span>5</span><p><strong>Boundary</strong><br />Have you avoided overgeneralising?</p></article>
            <article><span>6</span><p><strong>Citations</strong><br />Can readers trace each borrowed idea?</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Read the paragraph as a reader would: point, evidence, relationship, meaning, boundary and traceability.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>進行最後的段落審視</h2>
          <div class="paragraph-audit">
            <article><span>1</span><p><strong>觀點</strong><br />段落是否由一個清晰觀點控制？</p></article>
            <article><span>2</span><p><strong>選擇</strong><br />每個來源是否都服務該觀點？</p></article>
            <article><span>3</span><p><strong>綜合</strong><br />來源是否被比較，而不是羅列？</p></article>
            <article><span>4</span><p><strong>詮釋</strong><br />是否解釋了模式的意義？</p></article>
            <article><span>5</span><p><strong>邊界</strong><br />是否避免過度概括？</p></article>
            <article><span>6</span><p><strong>引用</strong><br />讀者能否追溯每個借用觀點？</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">以讀者的方式閱讀段落：觀點、證據、關係、意義、邊界與可追溯性。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

